! I-Box 1 diagnostic program, octal 5412.00 through 5461.40 -- FIVE
! consecutive test groups from docs/ja_ax1a_ibox-1.pdf pp.50-51,
! transcribed VERBATIM as one contiguous span at the listing's own
! addresses, with the deck's own pass/fail mechanism intact throughout:
!
!   SIC-CB      ISCB..ISCBH   5412.00   (same text as ibox1_sic_cb_cbz)
!   SIC-CBZ     ISCB5..ISCBK  5421.00
!   SIC-B,ZIND  ISBI..ISBXW   5432.40   SIC + Branch on Indicator ZERO
!   SIC-B,IND   ISBI5..ISBIK  5443.00   SIC + Branch on Indicator ONE
!   SIC-B,IND   WEN2/WEN/VEN  5454.00   (same text as verify_ibox1_listing's
!                                        WEN block; WEN6/WEN7 at 6102/6103)
!
! Control flow, as the deck wrote it: each group's SICs rewrite the
! "BD,$" hangs after them into "BD,<next hang>", the group ends by
! LV/SV-patching one more hang and walking the whole chain, and the
! chain's last hop lands on two VF words that decode as NOPs and fall
! into the next group. ISCBK's NOPs fall into ISBI at 5432.40; ISBIK's
! into WEN2 at 5454.00; VEN's own "BRGZZ,$+1.0" skips its hang into
! 5462.00, where the next test ("Y-Z CONTROL SEQUENCES", floating-
! point, out of this model's scope) begins -- the ONE substituted
! instruction here is a BEW,$ at that address. Any failure anywhere in
! the span hangs at a "BD,$" (a self-branch halts this model), so the
! testbench's PC check alone tells pass from fail; every rewritten hang
! is checked too (expected values from ibox1_expected.py).
!
! What the new groups exercise beyond ibox1_sic_cb_cbz.strap: SIC with
! a Branch-on-Indicator embedded (BZXF/BZXCZ/BZXVGZ/BZXVLZ taken when
! the indicator is OFF, BXF/BXCZ/BXVGZ not taken, BXVZ taken), which
! in turn requires LX to set the index flag and index result
! indicators from the loaded word (Reference Manual p.24: "the index-
! flag and index-result indicators are set in all of the preceding
! direct index arithmetic operations") -- ISBXW = XW,0,2,0 gives
! value 0, count 2, flag 0, so XVZ on and XF/XCZ/XVGZ/XVLZ off, as the
! listing's own comment on ISBI says. That indicator setting was
! MISSING from the model for every direct index op except V+/V+C/V+CR
! until this block was run (bsv/README.md, StretchExecute.bsv's
! DirIndex arm).
!
! Listing text restored from the printout's %..= to (..). One reading
! ambiguity: BZXVLZ,ISBI5's printed code is "5443.20 C0" or
! "5443.30 C0" on the scan; only .30 (indicator 49 = XVLZ) is
! consistent with the mnemonic and the model's indicator table, and
! that is what verify_ibox1_listing.py checks against.
!
! Bug injection, observed result: with LX's indicator setting removed
! again, 6 of 13 fail -- BZXF still branches (XF was off anyway), the
! stale XCZ from the preceding SV (X1's count is 0 there) makes BZXCZ
! fall through, and PC parks at ISBIC (5436.00), the hang after it;
! ISBIB/ISBIC/ISBID/ISBIH/ISBII are never rewritten. Reverted by
! un-patch; full suite green.

        SLC, (8)5412.0
ISCB    LCI,$X1,4           ! -SET UP COUNT
        NOP,0.0
ISCB1   SIC,ISCBA           ! -STORE IC,
        CB,$X1,ISCB2        ! -COUNT NOT 0,BRANCH
ISCBB   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISCBC
ISCB2   SIC,ISCBB           ! -STORE IC,
        CB,$X1,ISCB3        ! -COUNT NOT 0, BRANCH
ISCBC   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISCBD
ISCB3   SIC,ISCBC           ! -STORE IC,
        CB,$X1,ISCB4        ! -COUNT NOT 0, BRANCH
ISCBD   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISCBE
ISCB4   SIC,ISCBD           ! -STORE IC,
        CBZ,$X1,ISCB5       ! -COUNT ZERO, BRANCH
ISCBH   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISCBI
ISCB5   LCI,$X1,4           ! -SET UP COUNT
ISCB6   SIC,ISCBE           ! -DONT STORE IC
        CBZ,$X1,$+.32       ! -COUNT NOT ZERO NO BRANCH
ISCBE   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISCB7   SIC,ISCBF           ! -DONT STORE IC
        CBZ,$X1,$+.32       ! -COUNT NOT ZERO NO BRANCH
ISCBF   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISCB8   SIC,ISCBG           ! -DONT STORE IC
        CBZ,$X1,$+.32       ! -COUNT NOT ZERO, NO BRANCH
ISCBG   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISCB9   SIC,ISCBH           ! -STORE IC BECAUSE
        CBZ,$X1,$+1.0       ! -COUNT IS ZERO, BRANCH
ISCBI   BD,$                ! -BD, ISCBK (NEW ADDR)
        LV,$X1,ISCBJ        ! -SET UP ISCBI TO
        SV,$X1,ISCBI        ! -BRANCH OUT OF ROUTINE
ISCBA   BD,$                ! -BD,ISCBB (NEW ADDR)
ISCBJ   VF,ISCBK+.04        ! -ISCBI SET UP
ISCBK   VF,(8)777777.70     ! -NOP,-.32
        VF,(8)777777.70     ! -NOP,-.32
ISBI    LX,$X1,ISBXW        ! -XVZ ON, XCZ, XVGZ, XVLZ, XF OFF
        NOP
ISBI1   SIC,ISBIA           ! -STORE IC
        BZXF,ISBI2          ! -IND OFF, BRANCH
ISBIB   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISBIC
ISBI2   SIC,ISBIB           ! -STORE IC
        BZXCZ,ISBI3         ! -IND OFF, BRANCH
ISBIC   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISBID
ISBI3   SIC,ISBIC           ! -STORE IC
        BZXVGZ,ISBI4        ! -IND OFF, BRANCH
ISBID   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISBIE
ISBI4   SIC,ISBID           ! -STORE IC
        BZXVLZ,ISBI5        ! -IND OFF, BRANCH
ISBIH   BD,$                ! -HANG UP OR BECOME BD,ISBII
ISBXW   XW,0,2,0            ! -INDEX WORD
ISBI5   SIC,ISBIE           ! -DONT STORE IC
        BXF,$+.32           ! -IND OFF, NO BRANCH
ISBIE   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISBI6   SIC,ISBIF           ! -DONT STORE IC
        BXCZ,$+.32          ! -IND OFF, NO BRANCH
ISBIF   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISBI7   SIC,ISBIG           ! -DONT STORE IC
        BXVGZ,$+.32         ! -IND OFF, NO BRANCH
ISBIG   BD,$+.32            ! -HANG IF IC STORED
ISBI8   SIC,ISBIH           ! -STORE IC BECAUSE
        BXVZ,$+1.0          ! -XVZ IS ON, BRANCH
ISBII   BD,$                ! -BD, ISBIK (NEW ADDR)
        LV,$X1,ISBIJ        ! -SET UP ISBII TO
        SV,$X1,ISBII        ! -BRANCH OUT OF ROUTINE
ISBIA   BD,$                ! -BD, ISBIB (NEW ADDR)
ISBIJ   VF,ISBIK+.04        ! -ISBII SET UP
ISBIK   VF,(8)777777.70     ! -NOP,-.32
        VF,(8)777777.70     ! -NOP,-.32
WEN2    L(BU,64,8),WEN7     ! -LOAD ONES
        BRGZZ,$+1.0
        BD,$
WEN     L(BU,64,8),WEN6     ! -LOAD ZEROS
        BRZZ,$+1.0
        BD,$
VEN     L(BU,64,8),WEN7
        BRGZZ,$+1.0
        BD,$
IBY     BEW,$               ! substituted: "Y-Z CONTROL SEQUENCES" (FP) starts here
        SLC, (8)6102.0
WEN6    DD(BU,64,8), 0
WEN7    DD(BU,64,8), 18446744073709551615

        END, ISCB
